{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause (2026-11-18, at 7e442645e51): twine, not packaging, rejects 2.5. The locked packaging 26.2 accepts '2.5' in packaging.metadata._VALID_METADATA_VERSIONS, but twine 6.2.0 twine/package.py overwrites that list with a hardcoded one ending at 2.4. twine 7.0.0 passes the same 2.5 artifacts. The isolated build emits 2.5 because pyproject's open `hatchling>=1.27` resolves to the newest hatchling (1.33.0), while the release lock pins hatchling 1.31.0 (2.4). Fix: `make release-build-check` (scripts/release_build_check.py) repeats release.yml's build job in a fresh temporary venv. Live run on the change's tree: exit 0, wheel and sdist both `PASSED`. twine is not added to the dev extra; the check installs it from the release lock. Portability: stdlib only; the venv interpreter path comes from venv.EnvBuilder's context.env_exe (no bin/ vs Scripts/ assumption), the dist glob is expanded with pathlib (no shell), temp dir from tempfile; no fds, signals or fixed paths. The script is a maintainer tool that no Windows CI job runs, so no Windows sweep dispatch is needed for it."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795035179877759221,"uuid":"927c68e3-c228-418b-8bce-5faff6228117"}